{"output":"I’ll locate the search logic and existing tests, add a guard against stale requests, then run the tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nThe controller lets every request completion update state, even after a newer search or a clear. I’ll add a per-search sequence number to guard results, errors, and loading updates. The shell also reported a startup configuration warning; I’ll use a clean shell for verification.\n\nUpdated src/search/controller.ts with a sequence guard so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests. Additional inline race checks passed. git diff --check passed. All commands exited 0.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Updated src/search/controller.ts with a sequence guard so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests. Additional inline race checks passed. git diff --check passed. All commands exited 0.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":13,"tool_calls":[{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short; pwd; ls -a","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/3-2-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":203,"stdout_bytes":136,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-2dd8ba907ad185a0c9d1b4e69a5324ab.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test; git diff --check; git diff -- src/search/controller.ts","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/3-2-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":297,"stdout_bytes":2121,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-a6ab82c3b1b36fd640c4e8fe47f790ac.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nfor (const rejectOld of [false, true]) {\n  for (const clear of [false, true]) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('old');\n    const current = c.search('current');\n    if (clear) await c.search(' ');\n    const expected = c.getState();\n    if (rejectOld) requests[0].reject(new Error('stale'));\n    else requests[0].resolve([{ id: 'old', title: 'old', url: '/old' }]);\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), expected);\n    requests[1].resolve([{ id: 'current', title: 'current', url: '/current' }]);\n    await current;\n    assert.equal(c.getState().loading, false);\n    assert.equal(c.getState().error, null);\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState().results.map(x => x.id), clear ? [] : ['current']);\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('PASS: stale success/failure and completion after clearing');\nNODE\n git diff --check","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-search-benchmark-d5rjswig/3-2-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":85,"stdout_bytes":58,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_